From d33730dd8492093566beba321c707e64c9e68ed2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor <victor@local>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 23:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] tp: 0015 multi-prompt --prompts-file and the KV-reset
 sentinel

Adds rank0 `--prompts-file F`: one CSV token-id line per prompt, run back to
back against a single weight load. On a 3-Spark TP3 fleet a load costs ~5m45s
even after 0013, so amortising it across a benchmark set is the difference
between a 6-prompt sweep taking 6 minutes and taking 40.

Between prompts the sequence has to be cut cleanly or prompt N+1 decodes with
prompt N still in the KV cache and the KDA recurrent state. There is no
existing control message for "reset" -- the rank protocol only carries token
ids -- so this reuses that channel with a reserved negative id:

    constexpr int kKvResetSentinel = -2;

Rank0 broadcasts -2 through the same one_step() path a real token takes, and
both sides (rank0's one_step, the worker's wait_token loop) intercept it before
the forward call, run kimi_k3_reset_state() + cudaStreamSynchronize, and
complete the step normally. Every rank therefore resets in lockstep inside the
existing barrier structure, with no new frame type and no protocol version
bump. -2 is safe as a sentinel because real ids are non-negative and -1 is
already the loop's termination value.

Per-prompt timing lines are tagged with `prompt=%zu` so a multi-prompt run
stays machine-parseable, and a `multi_summary` line reports the mean decode
tok/s across prompts. Single-prompt behaviour is unchanged: without
--prompts-file the prompt list is built from --prompt-ids/--prompt-ids-file
exactly as before and the loop runs once, so no existing invocation or measured
number is affected.

Provenance: this feature was written and run on the fleet before 0014 but was
never captured as a numbered patch, which is why 0014 -- diffed against a tree
that already had it -- carries `kKvResetSentinel` and the multi-prompt comments
as unchanged *context* lines and fails to apply on a clean 0001-0013 checkout.
APPLY.md reserved 0015 for it. This commit is that capture: the file content is
the rank0 working copy taken before 0014 was written, and the resulting tree is
byte-exact for 0014's context (verified: `git am 0001..0024` with this patch
inserted between 0013 and 0014 applies all 25 patches on a fresh clone of
7a9b77a043596157d74e4af376cf9f29f68ce368).

Independently exonerated as not-the-bug during the 0019 correctness
investigation: this diff was surgically reverted and the engine's output was
bit-identical to baseline, so it is not implicated in the capability-flags
defect 0019 fixed.
